# .goalenv is PER-WORKTREE goal state: it cd's into ONE goal's worktree and pins that
# goal's allocated X display, OUT, RECON and HOME. Tracking it means the merge drops one
# goal's copy into every other goal's worktree, where `. ./.goalenv` then silently runs
# their commands in the WRONG TREE on the WRONG DISPLAY. It happened (2026-09-12 23:25).
# scripts/wt.sh writes it per worktree; it is never content to share.
.goalenv
